WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.404
NARRATOR: Neil and James search
a shipwreck for the mega shark

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.873
big bull, and other
large bull sharks

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.476
that may be her descendants.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.477
James, you okay?

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.979
I'm good over here.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.482
NARRATOR: Bull sharks have
a pack-like mentality,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:19.319
and swarm around possible food.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.754
They surround the divers.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.355
[panicked yelling]

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.457
I'm right behind you.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.859
Let's get to cover.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.795
NARRATOR: Neil and James nestle
into the wreck for protection.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.696
Yep.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.264
One's on your right.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.567
NARRATOR: Now, to get
some measurements.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.370
Neil, I'm going
to try and laser it.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.738
Get closer.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.474
NARRATOR: James's two lasers
work like an electronic ruler

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:45.612
to confirm the
size of the bulls.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:51.751
If one is close to 10 feet long,
it could be Big Bull, possibly

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.019
the largest shark alive.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.323
I've got the laser.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.592
I've got it locked on.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.362
Laser locked on.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.263
I've got it.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.964
I've got the shot.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.199
NARRATOR: There.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:09.269
Multiplying the 6 inch long
distance of the lasers,

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.971
they estimate that
this shark is young.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:15.308
From snout to the curve of
the tail, a little over 5

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.276
feet long.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.049
But nearby--

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.919
There's a big bull
shark over there.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.788
I'm going to try and
get our laser on it.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.123
I've got him.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.326
NARRATOR: A giant,
pushing 9 feet.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:40.200
Only inches smaller than
Big Bull was in 2012.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.835
They get more measurements.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.475
NARRATOR: But the strong
current, with this many sharks,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.644
turns this dive dangerous.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.779
Hey Neil, let's head up.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.251
This current is going to carry
me to England, otherwise.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.219
I'm with ya.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.029
How about that?

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.231
That was epic.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.999
Loads of bull sharks.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.601
Some nice-sized bulls.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.003
Not as big as Big Bull, but I
feel really good about this.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.838
It's a good starting point.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.607
We've taken the search
to the next level.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.975
NARRATOR: They've
confirmed bulls

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.545
as large as those reported by
local divers and fishermen.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.583
While they're not quite
the size of Big Bull,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.552
this is her territory.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.626
And if Neil's theory
is right, the sharks

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.562
here may be her offspring.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.665
[music playing]

